17.20 Mapping the Present Patient into the 180 Human Living Biological Network Systems
The Thirty-Nine Biological Axes provide an intermediate layer of biological interpretation.
However, disease ultimately manifests through disturbances occurring within the operational units of life itself.
Within the TSPI framework, these operational units are referred to as:
The 180 Human Living Biological Network Systems
The 180 Networks represent the distributed biological architecture through which energy, information, matter, adaptation, repair, and resilience are coordinated throughout the organism.
Unlike isolated molecular targets, these networks function as highly interconnected adaptive systems.
Consequently, disturbance within one network inevitably propagates throughout multiple neighboring networks.
The present patient therefore demonstrated not merely isolated abnormalities but widespread network-level disruption involving multiple interconnected biological domains.
