A shift from pursuing control toward cultivating harmony.
If such a transformation occurs, then the greatest achievement of medicine may not be the elimination of disease.
It may be the restoration of humanity's understanding of its place within the living network of life.

Final Reflection
We are not separate from life.
We are expressions of life.
We are not isolated systems.
We are living networks within larger living networks.
Our health depends upon those relationships.
Our resilience emerges from those relationships.
Our future depends upon those relationships.
And perhaps the deepest lesson of all is this:
To understand life is to understand relationship.
To preserve health is to preserve harmony.
To heal is to restore harmony where harmony has been lost.
The future of medicine begins there.
The future of humanity may as well.

